/// The MDI glyph tables HA's own frontend derives an icon from, vendored: per
/// device_class, per domain, and per state. Under `hass/` with the other HA
/// facts that go stale with a release (ADR 0015); a component author calls
/// [[core.icon.iconFor]] instead.
///
/// Only 24% of a real instance's entities carry an `icon`, and HA's derivation
/// of the rest never crosses the wire, so these draw three quarters of the
/// cards. MDI throughout, because that is what an entity's own `icon` names.
module hass_icons

/// Where the domain alone is too coarse; tried before [[domainIcons]]. One
/// table rather than one per domain: the overlap is small.
const deviceClassIcons: Mapping<String, String> = new {
  ["temperature"] = "mdi:thermometer"
  ["humidity"] = "mdi:water-percent"
